// deploy/vercel/function.tsconfig.json — the PREBUILT function's compiler
// config (T052 follow-up W-3k).
//
// deploy/vercel/build-console.mjs invokes tsc with THIS config to emit the
// CommonJS tree sealed inside .vercel/output/functions/api/router.func
// (the Build Output API v3 prebuilt deployment). It carries the laws the
// platform builder kept breaking, now owned by the build itself:
//
// THE W-3i LESSON (resolution): a builder's default synthesis
// (moduleResolution "nodenext") rejects the repo's extensionless relative
// imports (TS2835: "Relative import paths need explicit file extensions
// in ECMAScript imports...") and collapses services/api's types into
// cascade errors (TS2339/TS2322). node10 resolution ("node") keeps
// extensionless imports LEGAL — NEVER add extensions to the frozen
// services/api sources to satisfy a build tool.
//
// THE W-3j LESSON (emit): an ESM emit (`module: "ESNext"`) is UNLOADABLE
// at invoke time — extensionless specifiers Node cannot load
// (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND under ESM resolution; "Cannot use import
// statement outside a module" under CJS loading). The function must EMIT
// CommonJS (`module: "CommonJS"`; "Bundler" is invalid with CommonJS —
// TS5095 — so the pairing is node10).
//
// THE W-3k LESSON (the sealed scope): @vercel/node's emit copied the
// package.json files it encountered, so the emitted CJS graph's NEAREST
// package.json (services/api/package.json — "type": "module") made Node
// treat the CommonJS text as ESM: `ReferenceError: exports is not defined
// in ES module scope` at module load, every invocation 500
// (FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED). The tsc emit produces .js files ONLY —
// it copies nothing — and the .func is sealed by a root package.json
// with NO "type" field (pinned by deploy/vercel/vercel.test.ts: NO inner
// package.json anywhere in the .func).
//
// Under a CommonJS compile the vitest-only TEST sources are EXCLUDED
// (they carry import.meta — legal in the vitest ESM runtime, illegal
// under CommonJS: TS1343); tests are never part of the function's entry
// graph. THE EXCLUDE SCOPE LAW (W-3k, discovered by the failing first
// emit): exclude patterns resolve relative to THIS config file, so a
// bare "**/*.test.ts" matches nothing outside deploy/vercel/ — and the
// repo's test files DEEP-IMPORT the real packages (the interop
// trip-wires), which silently dragged packages/* + services/* into the
// emit. The exclude is therefore REPO-ROOT-scoped
// ("../../**/*.test.ts"), which keeps the program exactly the entry
// graph. The node ambient types are pinned EXPLICITLY (typeRoots
// relative to THIS file = the repo root's node_modules/@types — the
// same provision the platform's installCommand makes):
// runtime/http.ts (Buffer) and runtime/compose.ts (process) need them.
//
// rootDir = the repo root: the emit mirrors the repo layout inside the
// .func (deploy/vercel/api/router.js + deploy/vercel/runtime/*.js +
// services/api/src/*.js), which the sealed index.js requires verbatim.
// outDir below is the production .func path; the build script passes the
// same value as an explicit --outDir flag (hermetic builds may override).
{
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "CommonJS",
    "moduleResolution": "node",
    "typeRoots": ["../../node_modules/@types"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "noEmit": false,
    "rootDir": "../..",
    "outDir": "../../.vercel/output/functions/api/router.func"
  },
  "include": [
    "../../deploy/vercel/api/**/*.ts",
    "../../deploy/vercel/runtime/**/*.ts",
    "../../services/api/src/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["../../**/*.test.ts"]
}
